# The crown stops showing and starts bargaining. Fired once by
# MapComponent_TSC_Barrow, a little way into the barrow, at whichever
# companion is carrying shards. {PLAYER} is that carrier.
#
# Nothing mechanical is granted or lost here. The scene exists so that
# the ending choice is made by somebody who has already been offered the
# other thing and knows what refusing felt like.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_CrownOffer

== start ==
The pieces have gone quiet. Not silent: attentive: the hush before somebody important speaks.

And then it does speak, and it is not visions any more. It is words, in {PLAYER}'s own voice, using {PLAYER}'s own mannerisms. It is the most frightening thing that has happened on this journey.

It says: you are carrying more of me than anyone has held since the day I was split. Ask.

* "Ask for what?" -> what
* [Say nothing and keep walking.] -> walking

== walking ==
{PLAYER} keeps walking. The offer keeps pace, effortless, a current under the hull.

It is patient. It has been doing this a long time, and it has noticed that walking away is not the same as saying no.

* "Fine. Ask for what?" -> what

== what ==
Everything the carrier has actually wanted, laid out in order, and none of it is unreasonable.

Not thrones. Not armies. The small true things: the ones who did not make it out of the cellars. The company kept whole and paid. A road that stops being this hard. It knows them all, in detail, because it has been riding in a pack next to a beating heart for a long time and it has been listening.

Wear me, it says, and none of that is a wish any more.

* "You said that to the first king too." -> king
* "And what do you get?" -> price
* "No." -> refuse

== king ==
Yes, it agrees, without a flicker of shame. And he got all of it. So did the eleven who came after him, eleven of them inside a hundred years, every one of them brilliant and every one of them spent early.

None of them were lied to. Each was given exactly what they asked for.

They simply did not last very long, and it has never considered that the important part.

* "And what do you get?" -> price
* "No." -> refuse

== price ==
To be worn, it says.

That is the entire price and it is offered without any attempt to hide it. Somehow that is worse than a trick. It does not want power or worship or blood. It wants a head to sit on and hands to move, and it has been eight hundred years without either, and it is so tired of being carried in a bag.

* "No." -> refuse

== refuse ==
The offer withdraws. It does not sulk and it does not threaten; it simply files the answer away, creditor-patient, and moves on.

Then, mildly, as a last remark rather than a bargain:

You will be standing over an open coffin in a little while, holding all five of me, with your friends watching and no one left to stop you. We can talk again then.

The pieces go back to being cold weight in a pack, and the passage ahead goes back to being a passage.

* [Walk on.] -> end
    do grant_xp(50)
